# Field System Reference

## Overview

The field is the 2D drill field editor. It's drawn with three.js through React Three Fiber, behind an editor that owns every editing rule and knows nothing about the renderer ([ADR 0005](../../docs/adr/0005-three-field-renderer.md), [docs/field](../../docs/field/README.md)). An SVG overlay draws the selection box, handles, marquee, lasso and line-tool previews from the same editor state and view.

## Key Files

All under `apps/desktop/src/field/`.

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `editor/fieldEditor.ts` | The editor: presses, gestures, selection, live positions |
| `editor/selectionRules.ts`, `editor/selectionArea.ts` | Click, marquee and lasso rules |
| `editor/moveGesture.ts`, `editor/moveRules.ts` | Dragging marchers, snapping, Alt precision, locks |
| `editor/groupTransform.ts`, `editor/transformGestures.ts` | Scale and rotate handles |
| `editor/lineTool.ts` | The line tool (L) |
| `editor/view.ts` | Zoom, pan and their limits |
| `fieldDrop.ts` | Saves a drop through the drop-to-timeline planner |
| `fieldTestApi.ts`, `three/threeFieldTestApi.ts` | `window.fieldTest`, what scenario tests read |
| `three/ThreeField.tsx` | The field component (lazy-loaded from `App.tsx`) |
| `three/layers/*` | One component per layer: field, image, marchers, labels, overlays |
| `three/FieldOverlay.tsx` | The SVG overlay |
| `three/fieldView.ts` | The one view store the layers and the overlay read |
| `three/fieldMarchers.ts` | Where each marcher is drawn, outside React |
| `timelineOverlays.ts` | Pathways, the isolation scene and collision markers as plans |
| `fieldPlan.ts` | The field's layout, shared with the drill chart export |

## Rules

- Editing rules live in `editor/` (plain TypeScript), with Vitest tests in `editor/__test__/`.
- Draw on demand; one component per layer, never per marcher; write GPU buffers through refs from a frame hook or store subscription, never React state per frame.
- Scenario tests (`apps/desktop/e2e/browser/tests/`) check what the user sees and what gets saved, through `window.fieldTest` and saved data only, never three.js objects or shaders.
- The selection is the app's selection (`SelectedMarchersContext`); there is no separate field selection.
- App actions on the field on screen go through `activeFieldEditor()` (`selectAll`, `rotateSelection`).
